	<!--
	  Certificate pinning (#153, ADR-004, docs/CERTIFICATE-PINNING.md).
	  Every host FitBuddy sends a user secret to is pinned to the SPKI SHA-256
	  of its certificate authority's *root* key — not the leaf, not the
	  intermediate: Let's Encrypt and Google Trust Services rotate their
	  intermediates per issuance. Each host lists every root its CA (and, for
	  Cloudflare-fronted hosts, every CA Cloudflare may issue from) can chain
	  to, so a CA switch does not lock testers out. Derivation and the
	  rotation procedure are documented in docs/CERTIFICATE-PINNING.md;
	  CertificatePinningConfigurationTests guards this table.
	-->
